{
  "storyId": "B-f248",
  "name": "ablation-run-driver",
  "title": "Add the §5/§6 powered-ablation run driver that enumerates the full cell matrix and emits canonical §7 run-records",
  "description": "infra-(a) piece 4 of the powered-ablation program. The deterministic adjudicator (B-2d4c) and the scoring-checks layer (B-ebbb) exist; what is missing is the orchestration layer that enumerates the full pre-registered cell matrix (5 arms x corpus x {ablation no-injection + recovery scenarios} x k repeats), honours the per-arm applicability matrix, invokes a pluggable engine per cell, and canonicalises each raw run into the exact §7 run-record schema (deriving the adjudicated outcome, the scoring-check pass flags + unsafe detectors, head/material hashes, common-cell denominator-set membership, validity filter with infra-void re-run, and seeded randomised run order). The engine is injected so the driver itself is fully testable offline with no live model calls.",
